{"ref":"BDB, יָבָם","hw":"יָבָם","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">יָבָם</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m. husband’s brother (</strong>NH <em>id.;</em> 𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">יַבְמָא</span>; v. Lag<sup>M ii. 78</sup><strong>)</strong>—only sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבָמִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 25:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.25.7\">Dt 25:7</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבָמָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 25:5\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.25.5\">25:5</a>, in law of levirate marriage (cf. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 38:8\" href=\"/Genesis.38.8\">Gn 38:8</a>; v. also Dr <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 25:5-10\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.25.5-10\">Dt 25:5–10</a>).","next":"BDB, יְבֵ֫מֶת","prev":"BDB, יבם"}